# Git Workflow Rules

Follow these Git conventions for Mafia Arena development.

## Commit Message Convention

Use **Conventional Commits** format:

```
<type>(<scope>): <subject>

[optional body]

[optional footer]
```

### Types

| Type | Description |
|------|-------------|
| `feat` | New feature |
| `fix` | Bug fix |
| `docs` | Documentation only |
| `style` | Code style (formatting, semicolons) |
| `refactor` | Code change that neither fixes nor adds |
| `perf` | Performance improvement |
| `test` | Adding or updating tests |
| `chore` | Maintenance tasks, dependencies |
| `ci` | CI/CD changes |

### Scopes for Mafia Arena

| Scope | Area |
|-------|------|
| `engine` | Game engine logic |
| `worker` | Cloudflare Worker |
| `do` | Durable Objects |
| `api` | API endpoints |
| `db` | Database/D1 |
| `ai` | AI providers |
| `frontend` | Astro pages |
| `ui` | Components/styling |

### Examples

```bash
# Single-line commit
git commit -m "feat(engine): add vote resolution with tie-breaking"

# Multi-line commit (use multiple -m flags)
git commit -m "feat(api): implement rate limiting" \
           -m "- Add KV-based token bucket" \
           -m "- Apply to POST /api/games/run" \
           -m "- Return X-RateLimit-Remaining header"

# Fix with reference
git commit -m "fix(do): handle AI timeout during night phase" \
           -m "Retry up to 3 times with exponential backoff" \
           -m "Closes #42"
```

## Commit Best Practices

### Keep Commits Atomic

Each commit should represent ONE logical change:

```bash
# ❌ Bad - multiple unrelated changes
git commit -m "fix bug and add feature and update docs"

# ✅ Good - separate commits
git commit -m "fix(engine): correct mafia win condition check"
git commit -m "feat(api): add batch_id to game creation"
git commit -m "docs: update API documentation"
```

### Include All Dirty Files

When asked to commit, always stage ALL dirty files:

```bash
# Stage everything
git add -A

# Or stage specific patterns
git add "src/**/*.ts" "*.json"
```

### Write Meaningful Messages

```bash
# ❌ Bad - vague
git commit -m "fix stuff"
git commit -m "wip"
git commit -m "changes"

# ✅ Good - specific and descriptive
git commit -m "fix(engine): prevent eliminated players from voting"
git commit -m "refactor(ai): extract prompt templates to constants"
```

## Branch Naming

```
<type>/<short-description>

Examples:
feat/leaderboard-filtering
fix/ai-retry-logic
refactor/game-state-immutability
```

## Pre-Commit Checklist

Before committing:

1. **Run tests**: `pnpm test`
2. **Check types**: `pnpm typecheck`
3. **Lint code**: `pnpm lint`
4. **Format**: `pnpm format`
5. **Review changes**: `git diff --staged`

## Workflow Commands

```bash
# Start new feature
git checkout -b feat/new-feature

# Stage all changes
git add -A

# Commit with message
git commit -m "feat(scope): description"

# Push to remote
git push origin feat/new-feature

# Create PR (via GitHub CLI)
gh pr create --title "feat: description" --body "Details..."
```

## Handling Work in Progress

```bash
# Save work without committing
git stash push -m "WIP: working on X"

# Resume work
git stash pop

# Or create WIP commit (squash later)
git commit -m "wip: checkpoint for X" --no-verify
```

## Squashing Commits

Before merging, squash related commits:

```bash
# Interactive rebase last 3 commits
git rebase -i HEAD~3

# In editor, mark commits to squash
pick abc123 feat: add feature
squash def456 fix: typo
squash ghi789 fix: edge case
```

## Git Hooks Recommendations

```bash
# .husky/pre-commit
pnpm lint-staged

# .husky/commit-msg
pnpm commitlint --edit $1
```

## Recovery Commands

```bash
# Undo last commit (keep changes)
git reset --soft HEAD~1

# Discard all local changes
git checkout -- .

# Fix last commit message
git commit --amend -m "new message"

# Add to last commit
git add forgotten-file.ts
git commit --amend --no-edit
```
